       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Labeled maximum:** The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for some formulations). Doses are usually divided into 500\u20131,000 mg per administration.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and they give no added glycemic benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), or\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day), or\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** at a different frequency, or\n- **170 mg**, if there was a decimal slip?\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that the dose was confirmed as intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
